# Citation metadata for the KerrRay software (https://citation-file-format.github.io).
# The DOI is that of the archived GitHub release v0.1.1 on Zenodo.
# Once the paper has an arXiv identifier, add a preferred-citation block for it.
cff-version: 1.2.0
doi: "10.5281/zenodo.23051526"
repository-code: "https://github.com/joelprince2601/kerrray"
date-released: "2026-09-30"
message: "If you use KerrRay, please cite it using these metadata."
type: software
title: "KerrRay: a CPU ray tracer for photon geodesics in Kerr spacetime"
version: "v0.1.1"
license: MIT
authors:
  - family-names: Prince
    given-names: Joel
abstract: >-
  KerrRay integrates null geodesics of the Kerr metric in Hamiltonian form in
  Boyer-Lindquist coordinates with an adaptive Dormand-Prince 5(4) scheme,
  with NumPy and Numba backends. It is the code behind the study "How
  accurate is a numerically reconstructed Kerr black-hole shadow?
  Resolution, tolerance and integration failures in an open CPU ray tracer",
  which measures the error of reconstructed shadow edges against the
  analytic Bardeen curve.
keywords:
  - general relativity
  - Kerr black hole
  - black-hole shadow
  - null geodesics
  - ray tracing
  - numerical methods
